@buyaa-n the error message of `Assert.NotEqual()` is confusing.
The test case says that Get and Set should NOT be EQUAL, but it fails.

The other assertions fail as well:
```
var get = type.GetMethod("Get");
var set = type.GetMethod("Set");
// get and set should not be equal.
// all assertions below fail for array types loaded by MetadataLoadContext.
Asssert.False(get.Equals(set));
Asssert.True(get != set);
Asssert.False(get == set);
```

@buyaa-n @steveharter thank you for fixing. And I'm sorry to be late for commenting.

Look carefully at 'Other information' of the issue.
I think the problem is that RoArrayType.GetMethodsCore() assigns new uniquifiers from zero for every call, which vary depending on the filter.

The following assertion would fail because the uniquifier of the left side is 0 and that of the right side is 1.
```
var t = typeof(int[]).Project();
Assert.Equal(t.GetMethod("Set"), t.GetMethods().First(x => x.Name == "Set"));
```

An easy way would be to assign constant uniquifiers to Get/Set/Address.
